# Performance Standards

Performance is a feature.

Every implementation should consider:

Speed

Responsiveness

Efficiency

Scalability

---

# Lighthouse Goals

Performance

95+

Accessibility

100

Best Practices

100

SEO

100

---

# Images

Always optimize images.

Prefer:

AVIF

↓

WebP

↓

JPEG

Use responsive images.

Lazy load images below the fold.

Never serve oversized assets.

---

# Video

Compress videos.

Use autoplay only when muted.

Use poster images.

Lazy load when possible.

---

# Fonts

Load only required weights.

Use next/font.

Avoid render blocking.

---

# Components

Prefer Server Components.

Client Components only when necessary.

---

# Rendering

Prefer:

SSR

↓

RSC

↓

CSR

Only use CSR where interaction is required.

---

# Bundle Size

Avoid unnecessary dependencies.

Prefer tree-shakable libraries.

---

# API

Cache appropriate requests.

Paginate large datasets.

Never fetch unnecessary data.

---

# Database

Avoid N+1 queries.

Optimize indexes.

Paginate results.

---

# Animation

Animations must never block interaction.

Respect reduced-motion settings.

---

# Goal

Fast enough that users never notice waiting.